WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.679 --> 00:00:08.780
The most money ever paid for a cow in an auction
was $1.3 million.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:15.250
Welcome to RIF.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:21.440
In the US, The Eisenhower interstate system
requires that one mile in every five must

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.820
be straight.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:28.710
These straight sections are usable as airstrips
in times of war or other emergencies.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:33.530
If you get burnt, crack open an egg, peel
the egg's membrane from the inside of the

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:36.380
shell and place it over the wound.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.160
The wound will heal without scarring.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:45.970
Neanderthal's brains were bigger than modern
humans, they just lacked the necessary social

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.600
skills to thrive.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:54.640
On average, people swallow 1.5 litres of urine
when swimming in a public pool.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.540
Also the Romans used to make toothpaste from
urine.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:03.200
The Australian $5 to $100 notes are made of
plastic.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:09.860
Dueling is legal in Paraguay as long as both
parties are registered blood donors.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:16.860
If you try to suppress a sneeze, you can rupture
a blood vessel in your head or neck and die.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:25.420
Wearing headphones for just an hour will increase
the bacteria in your ear by 700 times.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:31.910
Rats multiply so quickly that in 18 months,
two rats could have over a million descendants.

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:54.179
And finally, there is a town in Norway called
Hell, and it freezes over almost every winter.

